{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01XKKoVPerhUBiCnH9sN8Lor","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the project's own documents (CLAUDE.md, the locked North Stars, and the declared deliverable), here is what Anchor **is**:\n\n- **It's a personal productivity / task-management system for J.C. Liechty**, living entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) with **plain markdown files as the single source of truth** â€” no database, no syncing. Tasks, projects, inbox, and archives are all markdown (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files), each task carrying priority/energy/domain/due/notes fields and moving through a lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled / saved-for-later â†’ restored).\n\n- **What it ships is `anchor_gui.py`** (the one declared deliverable): a self-contained, **Python-stdlib-only local web server** that runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`, regenerates the full dashboard HTML on each request, and writes changes straight back to the markdown via a small `/api/*` REST surface. A CLI engine (`anchor.py`) mirrors the same logic and emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Beyond plain task tracking, it has grown an \"R&D Control Surface\"** â€” a per-project cockpit for running the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman trio** (research/planning/build) as durable, server-side AI sessions. Each project window shows lanes as tiles with honest status lights, expands inline panels with cached summaries plus a live terminal, and tracks sessions, deliverables, and a cost/tokens/time rollup. This has been built and merged through **four versions** (v2 sessions/summaries â†’ v3 \"Mission Control\" â†’ v4 \"Project Cockpit\", merged to master 2026-06-13).\n\n- **The terminal substrate is real ConPTY** (xterm.js over WebSocket/SSE, with git-worktree isolation per session) â€” this is the **single declared exception** to the otherwise-strict stdlib-only / no-native-assets rule, via an optional lazy `pywinpty` import in `pty_manager.py`. Everything else stays pure stdlib, enforced by `distro.py`'s import scan.\n\n- **It's self-verifying:** a daily 5 AM health-check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint, and walks the full v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces with all model calls stubbed â€” surfacing a red dashboard banner on any failure.\n\nIn short: Anchor is a markdown-backed, stdlib-only local web app that doubles as a personal task dashboard **and** a mission-control cockpit for driving AI-assisted R&D projects through a researchâ†’planâ†’build pipeline."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1627aaa8-736f-4264-a5da-5a8ddbe0bcfd","uuid":"fd57b610-17a4-4fe3-b1ab-aeeb98259f4d","request_id":"req_011Cc1fS5VhwRWt1nrh3Vkbv"}
